WEBVTT


00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:04.793
[eerie instrumental music]


00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:12.902
¶ ¶


00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.352
[labored breathing]


00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:39.561
[clicking noise]


00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:50.773
- Listen.


00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:58.013
Listen.


00:01:03.797 --> 00:01:06.789
Do you hear it?


00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:15.739
Go away.


00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:17.639
You all have to go away.


00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:20.645
[gasping breaths]


00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:23.739
[strange scraping noises]


00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:29.413
No!


00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:33.458
[footsteps pounding]


00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:36.552
[locks clicking]


00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:48.364
It's not in my head.


00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:50.375
Bobby.


00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:53.469
Bobby, where are you?


00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:58.173
Bobby.


00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:01.447
Bobby, why aren't you here?


00:02:05.692 --> 00:02:07.819
It's happening again.


00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:10.191
Shh, shh.


00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:13.390
[whimpering]


00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:16.492
They're after me.


00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.999
I'm not crazy.
I'm not crazy.


00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:25.634
You hear them, don't you?


00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:28.737
[labored breathing]


00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:36.784
No.


00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:37.879
No!


00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:42.519
[sobbing and screaming]


00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:45.621
[pounding noises]


00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:49.925
[gagging]


00:02:57.010 --> 00:03:00.002
[keys jangling]


00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:05.807
buzz!


00:03:05.919 --> 00:03:08.911
[mechanical whirring]


00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.688
- Well, they're hiring
non-unions


00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:18.457
down at sanitation,
if you're interested.


00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:21.797
- There's nothing
in transportation?


00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:22.890
- Not at the moment.


00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:26.529
Do you have any other
job skills?


00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:28.800
- Good mechanic.


00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:32.935
- Got a lot of mechanics waiting
for work already.


00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:36.379
All right, now what time will l
expect you to call me tonight?


00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:39.110
- About what?


00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:40.846
- Well, it says here you got
a board release.


00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:42.979
Do you understand
what that means?


00:03:45.425 --> 00:03:46.687
- I've never done this before.


00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:49.318
- It means parole
on a short leash.


00:03:49.429 --> 00:03:50.418
So you call


00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.225
in the next 24 hours
and let me know


00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:53.959
where you're parking
yourself tonight.


00:03:55.435 --> 00:03:58.268
- I'm staying at my mother's.


00:03:58.371 --> 00:03:59.360
- All right.


00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:03.738
You come in every Tuesday
for the next six months.


00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:06.209
Now, this is important,
because you miss one,


00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:09.247
you're in violation.


00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:10.976
Does your mother know
you're staying with her?


00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:12.073
- No.


00:04:12.185 --> 00:04:15.677
- Well, don't you think
you should call and tell her?


00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:18.222
- She died while I was inside.


00:04:20.627 --> 00:04:21.616
- I'm sorry to hear that.


00:04:21.728 --> 00:04:24.492
Do you have any other family?


00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:30.859
Call him in the morning.


00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:32.961
He may have work.


00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:34.232
Not a lot of employers


00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.706
want to hire people
in your situation.


00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:12.534
[horn honking]


00:05:21.621 --> 00:05:24.613
[men talking indistinctly]


00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:48.570
buzz!


00:06:00.293 --> 00:06:01.317
- Need something?


00:06:03.296 --> 00:06:04.627
- Helen Reynolds' son.


00:06:04.731 --> 00:06:05.720
I left you that message.


00:06:05.832 --> 00:06:06.821
- Oh, yeah, yeah.


00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:10.027
Of course, 519.


00:06:10.136 --> 00:06:13.128
Wait here.


00:06:24.584 --> 00:06:26.609
- I don't know where I'm going.


00:06:26.719 --> 00:06:28.186
- Elevator to five.


00:06:30.957 --> 00:06:34.188
Had to go in to change
the locks, you know?


00:06:34.293 --> 00:06:35.282
- How come?


00:06:35.395 --> 00:06:36.987
- Well, the police had to break
the door open,


00:06:37.096 --> 00:06:39.121
you know, when they found her.


00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:41.359
I didn't charge you for it,
though.


00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:43.298
- Thanks.


00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:57.043
- [muttering in Russian]


00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:58.777
- Going up?


00:06:58.885 --> 00:07:01.877
- [muttering in Russian]


00:07:36.956 --> 00:07:39.948
[door creaks]


00:07:53.639 --> 00:07:55.630
[metal scrapes]


00:08:02.849 --> 00:08:05.784
[high-pitched discordant
piano music]


00:08:05.885 --> 00:08:13.883
¶ ¶


00:08:31.944 --> 00:08:33.935
[sighs]


00:08:42.788 --> 00:08:45.780
[muffled voices]


00:08:53.432 --> 00:09:01.430
¶ ¶


00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:43.632
- [sighs]


00:10:54.887 --> 00:10:57.788
[sweet piano music]


00:10:57.890 --> 00:11:05.888
¶ ¶


00:11:05.998 --> 00:11:08.990
[thumping and scraping]


00:11:48.774 --> 00:11:50.799
Ow!


00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:51.934
Damn it.


00:12:20.706 --> 00:12:21.798
- What do you mean,
what do I mean?


00:12:21.907 --> 00:12:22.896
Where were you?


00:12:23.008 --> 00:12:25.476
- I was just here
inside the house.


00:12:25.578 --> 00:12:27.068
- You were just here inside
of the house.


00:12:27.179 --> 00:12:28.612
Now, how come I saw you
out by that door?


00:12:28.714 --> 00:12:31.046
What are you doing at that door?


00:12:35.621 --> 00:12:36.610
You weren't there?


00:12:36.722 --> 00:12:39.714
What, am I seeing things?


00:12:58.043 --> 00:13:00.068
- I really don't understand.


00:13:00.179 --> 00:13:01.271
What happened here?


00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:03.405
[mumbling]


00:13:13.793 --> 00:13:16.785
[door slams]


00:13:18.697 --> 00:13:21.257
Oh, there's another story again.


00:13:21.367 --> 00:13:22.459
- No, it's not a story.


00:13:22.568 --> 00:13:24.627
She wanted to play.


00:13:24.737 --> 00:13:26.068
- She can play inside
the apartment.


00:13:26.172 --> 00:13:29.767
Why do you have to play with her
out in the hallway?


00:13:29.875 --> 00:13:32.867
[record skips]


00:14:22.461 --> 00:14:25.453
[muffled voices]


00:14:26.765 --> 00:14:29.757
[people chattering]


00:14:49.321 --> 00:14:52.415
- I'll be right with you.


00:14:52.524 --> 00:14:53.582
- What do you guys want?


00:14:53.692 --> 00:14:54.681
- Tell me what's good here.


00:14:54.793 --> 00:14:57.694
- Listen.


00:14:57.796 --> 00:14:59.957
Hey.


00:15:02.001 --> 00:15:06.062
- Can you excuse me?


00:15:06.171 --> 00:15:07.297
Hi.


00:15:10.609 --> 00:15:12.008
When did you get back?


00:15:13.779 --> 00:15:15.041
- A couple days.


00:15:16.181 --> 00:15:17.705
- Are you here for good?


00:15:18.684 --> 00:15:19.708
- I hope so.


00:15:24.456 --> 00:15:25.445
- I'm sorry about your mom.


00:15:25.557 --> 00:15:29.049
I heard what happened.


00:15:29.161 --> 00:15:33.120
- Yeah, it's...


00:15:33.232 --> 00:15:34.221
You look great.


00:15:34.333 --> 00:15:36.164
- No, no, I don't.


00:15:36.268 --> 00:15:37.701
You don't have to say that.


00:15:39.071 --> 00:15:41.096
- Maybe a cup of coffee
or something later?


00:15:41.206 --> 00:15:43.106
- I can't.
I have finals.


00:15:43.208 --> 00:15:45.108
- School?
You're going to school?


00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:46.643
- Yep.


00:15:46.745 --> 00:15:48.337
- That's amazing.


00:15:48.447 --> 00:15:50.472
- I have to design
an entire line by next week.


00:15:50.582 --> 00:15:53.415
It's...


00:15:53.519 --> 00:15:55.248
everything's really different
for me now.


00:15:55.354 --> 00:15:56.582
- Yeah, maybe another time.


00:15:56.689 --> 00:15:58.782
Maybe this weekend, maybe-


00:15:58.891 --> 00:16:01.052
- I'm working doubles
and school,


00:16:01.160 --> 00:16:03.754
and, look,
I have zero free time.


00:16:05.664 --> 00:16:07.097
I don't think it's a good idea.


00:16:08.100 --> 00:16:09.965
- Can we get the bill, please?


00:16:10.069 --> 00:16:11.093
- [sighs]


00:16:11.203 --> 00:16:12.192
I'm sorry.


00:16:12.304 --> 00:16:15.137
I have to get back to work.


00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:16.229
- It's good to see you.


00:16:16.342 --> 00:16:17.331
- You too.


00:16:42.601 --> 00:16:45.161
[scraping noises]


00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:48.262
[person moaning]


00:16:57.449 --> 00:17:00.441
[louder moaning]


00:17:11.430 --> 00:17:14.763
[gasping]


00:17:21.974 --> 00:17:24.966
[clattering noise]


00:17:26.645 --> 00:17:28.169
- Help.
- Mom.


00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:30.475
- Help me.


00:17:33.052 --> 00:17:36.044
[heavy breathing]


00:17:44.163 --> 00:17:47.155
[men talking indistinctly]


00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:51.667
- See anything wrong?


00:17:51.770 --> 00:17:54.500
- Got to be a loose
brake pad spring.


00:17:54.606 --> 00:17:55.595
- You're sure about that?


00:17:55.707 --> 00:17:56.765
- Guy complained of a rattle


00:17:56.875 --> 00:17:58.365
when he drives over bumps,
right?


00:17:58.477 --> 00:18:00.104
- That's right.


00:18:00.212 --> 00:18:02.407
You know how to check for
misfires in alignment pressure?


00:18:02.514 --> 00:18:06.450
- Yeah.


00:18:08.487 --> 00:18:10.478
- Look, I've got to be honest
with you.


00:18:11.623 --> 00:18:12.612
Involuntary manslaughter,


00:18:12.724 --> 00:18:14.157
that's not exactly
a minor offense, you know?


00:18:14.259 --> 00:18:16.659
- If I had more to offer you
than my word,


00:18:16.762 --> 00:18:17.751
I would give it to you, man.


00:18:17.863 --> 00:18:22.857
But I'm just trying to put
my life back together.


00:18:25.003 --> 00:18:25.992
- Pay ain't high.


00:18:26.105 --> 00:18:28.665
- I don't need much.


00:18:30.209 --> 00:18:33.201
- If I hire you, I just ask you
to be straight with me.


00:18:33.312 --> 00:18:34.370
All right?


00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:35.947
It took me a long time
to build this shop,


00:18:36.048 --> 00:18:37.413
and I don't want anything
risking that.


00:18:37.516 --> 00:18:38.505
You understand?


00:18:38.617 --> 00:18:42.553
- Give me one week,
and I'll show you what I can do.


00:18:42.654 --> 00:18:44.554
- Come back tomorrow.


00:18:44.656 --> 00:18:45.645
- Thank you.


00:18:45.757 --> 00:18:48.317
- All right.


00:18:48.427 --> 00:18:49.724
Sir, get up.


00:19:00.072 --> 00:19:02.870
buzz!


00:19:02.975 --> 00:19:07.309
- It's suppertime.


00:19:07.412 --> 00:19:08.436
He won't answer.


00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:14.214
- Got some plumbing problems,
I think.


00:19:14.319 --> 00:19:17.220
Like, I'm hearing noises
in the walls.


00:19:33.138 --> 00:19:34.127
- Patrol and unit 25.


00:19:34.239 --> 00:19:37.936
[indistinct]


00:19:38.043 --> 00:19:41.035
- [woman speaks indistinctly]


00:19:45.817 --> 00:19:47.182
- We get calls.


00:19:47.286 --> 00:19:51.950
This is a code four
on First and Broadway.


00:19:52.057 --> 00:19:53.046
- Code two.


00:19:53.158 --> 00:19:55.752
Get 6544.


00:20:07.306 --> 00:20:10.298
[indistinct voices over radio]


00:20:30.829 --> 00:20:32.922
- [sighs]


00:20:33.031 --> 00:20:35.363
Great.


00:20:37.035 --> 00:20:40.300
[cheers and applause on TV]


00:20:40.405 --> 00:20:42.373
Miss Trupiano?


00:20:42.474 --> 00:20:44.840
Bobby Reynolds.


00:20:44.943 --> 00:20:45.932
Yeah.


00:20:46.044 --> 00:20:47.636
Yeah, from high school.


00:20:47.746 --> 00:20:52.683
Uh, yeah, I was released.


00:20:52.784 --> 00:20:55.514
Is Louis there?


00:20:55.621 --> 00:20:57.521
Oh, yeah?


00:20:57.623 --> 00:21:01.389
You got a forwarding number
maybe or-


00:21:01.493 --> 00:21:04.053
Hello?


00:21:04.162 --> 00:21:07.154
Hello?


00:21:10.769 --> 00:21:12.566
- She's got the dirty mouth
from the South.


00:21:12.671 --> 00:21:14.571
All the way from Pascagoula,
Mississippi,


00:21:14.673 --> 00:21:15.970
it's Molly Ritter.


00:21:16.074 --> 00:21:19.066
[cheers and applause]


00:21:28.387 --> 00:21:31.379
[dull scraping]


00:21:38.897 --> 00:21:41.889
[dull scraping]


00:22:01.953 --> 00:22:04.945
[muffled scraping]


00:22:31.450 --> 00:22:34.010
[high-pitched piano tone]


00:22:56.775 --> 00:22:59.767
[lid creaks]


00:23:08.353 --> 00:23:09.650
[high-pitched piano tone]


00:23:31.610 --> 00:23:34.272
You handle all the apartments
in the building, man?


00:23:34.379 --> 00:23:35.641
Who's been in mine?


00:23:35.747 --> 00:23:37.476
- You have the only key.


00:23:37.582 --> 00:23:39.413
Everything okay?


00:23:42.154 --> 00:23:43.883
- I found these.


00:23:47.592 --> 00:23:48.581
- They're fingernails.


00:23:48.693 --> 00:23:49.819
- I know what they are, man.


00:23:49.928 --> 00:23:51.190
Why-why are they in my place?


00:23:51.296 --> 00:23:52.285
Who would keep 'em?


00:23:52.397 --> 00:23:54.558
- Maybe they belong
to your mother?


00:23:54.666 --> 00:23:55.997
- Why would she keep 'em?


00:23:57.836 --> 00:23:59.064
- When did you
speak to her last?


00:24:01.339 --> 00:24:02.328
- Couple of years.


00:24:02.441 --> 00:24:05.001
Yeah, you shouldn't have
to hear this from me,


00:24:05.110 --> 00:24:07.806
but the neighbors heard
from the police.


00:24:07.913 --> 00:24:10.848
Your mother locked herself
in her apartment for weeks


00:24:10.949 --> 00:24:14.407
before she died.


00:24:14.519 --> 00:24:17.886
- What?


00:24:17.989 --> 00:24:19.513
You got any idea
why she would do that?


00:24:19.624 --> 00:24:21.387
- No idea.


00:24:21.493 --> 00:24:22.824
I started work here after.


00:24:22.928 --> 00:24:24.395
I never met her.


00:24:24.496 --> 00:24:26.987
But when they found her,
she was in real bad shape.


00:24:27.098 --> 00:24:30.329
You never knew about this?


00:24:30.435 --> 00:24:32.494
Nobody check in on her?


00:24:32.604 --> 00:24:36.404
- She didn't have
anybody else, man.


00:24:36.508 --> 00:24:38.169
Maybe one of the neighbors
upstairs knows more.


00:24:38.276 --> 00:24:39.265
- Well, no offense, son,


00:24:39.377 --> 00:24:41.277
but nobody here wants
to talk to you.


00:24:41.379 --> 00:24:43.677
Everybody knows you were
in prison.


00:24:43.782 --> 00:24:45.682
People talk.


00:24:45.784 --> 00:24:47.877
She was sick, real sick.


00:24:47.986 --> 00:24:48.975
- Yeah.


00:24:49.087 --> 00:24:50.816
You-you gonna check
on those noises?


00:24:50.922 --> 00:24:51.946
- What noises?


00:24:52.057 --> 00:24:53.388
- In the walls.


00:24:53.492 --> 00:24:54.550
Rusty pipes, I don't know.


00:24:54.659 --> 00:24:56.752
They're coming
from somewhere, man.


00:24:56.862 --> 00:24:58.727
Well, this is a prewar building.


00:24:58.830 --> 00:24:59.990
You know, walls are thick.


00:25:00.098 --> 00:25:01.793
There's vents running through
the ceiling.


00:25:01.900 --> 00:25:03.527
There's no sound.


00:25:03.635 --> 00:25:07.765
You seem to be the only one
hearing things.


00:25:17.616 --> 00:25:19.516
- I wasn't there.
- You weren't there?


00:25:19.618 --> 00:25:22.849
What am l-
am I seeing things?


00:25:22.954 --> 00:25:24.546
- l-I don't know what you're
talking about.


00:25:24.656 --> 00:25:26.556
- Why do you keep lying to me
all the time?


00:25:26.658 --> 00:25:27.647
- I'm not lying to you.


00:25:27.759 --> 00:25:28.817
What, I go to work all day.


00:25:28.927 --> 00:25:30.121
I come home and what?


00:25:30.228 --> 00:25:31.286
- No, just just stop.


00:25:31.396 --> 00:25:32.385
- Who is this guy?


00:25:32.497 --> 00:25:33.486
- Stop.


00:25:33.598 --> 00:25:34.622
Stop it.


00:25:34.733 --> 00:25:36.132
Please.


00:25:36.234 --> 00:25:38.099
- Well, you're acting like I'm-
what, like-what am l?


00:25:38.203 --> 00:25:39.192
Am I the bad guy here?


00:25:39.304 --> 00:25:40.362
You're the one that's out-


00:25:40.472 --> 00:25:41.598
- No, no, no, no,
I didn't say that.


00:25:41.706 --> 00:25:42.695
I didn't say it.


00:25:42.807 --> 00:25:44.365
- Well, what the hell
were you doing there?


00:25:44.476 --> 00:25:46.239
- I wasn't doing anything.


00:25:46.344 --> 00:25:48.005
- I don't want to catch you
by that door again.


00:25:48.113 --> 00:25:51.105
- Are you all right in there?


00:26:08.366 --> 00:26:10.766
[power tools whining]


00:26:10.869 --> 00:26:12.598
- All right, we'll start you off
with tune-ups.


00:26:12.704 --> 00:26:14.035
We'll see how fast you work.


00:26:14.139 --> 00:26:16.039
You're also going to bring
the cars in and park them


00:26:16.141 --> 00:26:17.335
behind the gate every night.


00:26:17.442 --> 00:26:19.034
It's freshman work,
but you're the new guy.


00:26:19.144 --> 00:26:20.202
You show me you got skills,


00:26:20.312 --> 00:26:21.870
I'll give you more shifts
and bigger jobs.


00:26:21.980 --> 00:26:23.413
- You hear that?


00:26:23.515 --> 00:26:26.211
- What?


00:26:26.318 --> 00:26:27.717
- Like a voice.


00:26:27.819 --> 00:26:29.480
- It's a valve grinder.


00:26:29.588 --> 00:26:33.149
Car keys are in there.


00:26:35.393 --> 00:26:37.623
[woman whimpering]


00:26:37.729 --> 00:26:39.094
- What is that?


00:26:39.197 --> 00:26:40.562
- That's the drop-box.


00:26:40.665 --> 00:26:44.362
Don't give keys out till
the customer's paid in full.


00:26:44.469 --> 00:26:45.458
You got it?


00:26:45.570 --> 00:26:48.300
